# Generic rules-engine plugins

Every rules-engine plugin must implement reusable game behavior. A plugin must
not identify, branch on, or be named after one specific card.

- Describe card-specific abilities declaratively in `cardPlugins/cardRules.ts`.
- Give a unique card ability a specific effect-constructor name when that makes
  the card rule readable.
- Parameterize the generic instruction or handler that executes the effect.
- Plugins may inspect effect parameters, events, zones, types, and source IDs;
  they must not inspect a source's card name to decide what behavior to run.
- Add regression coverage that exercises the card rule through the generic
  trigger and resolution paths.
